 "tasks": {
  "essays": {
   "name": "Essay",
   "exam": "both",
   "line": "Part 1 · compulsory · 140–190 words · about 40 minutes",
   "brief": "You get a question and three notes: two given, one your own. Write one paragraph for each note.",
   "reader": "Your teacher · semi-formal: no slang, no contractions",
   "routes": [
    {
     "id": "say",
     "name": "Say what you think",
     "when": "Most questions. You agree (or disagree) and all three notes back you up."
    },
    {
     "id": "both",
     "name": "Both sides, then decide",
     "when": "When one of the notes argues against the others."
    }
   ],
   "questions": {
    "src": "/skills/writing/essays/data/essay-questions.json",
    "kind": "essay"
   },
   "bands": [
    {
     "job": "Hook + say your plan",
     "label": "Introduction",
     "words": 30,
     "steps": [
      {
       "label": "Hook",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "People often disagree about [topic].",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "These days, [topic] is something many young people talk about."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Your answer",
       "route": "say",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "In my opinion,",
         "h": "+ your answer",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "I strongly believe that",
         "h": "+ your answer"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Your plan",
       "route": "both",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "In this essay, I will look at both sides before giving my own view.",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "There are good arguments on both sides, so let's look at each one."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "job": "Note 1 · a reason + an example",
     "label": "Paragraph 2",
     "words": 40,
     "support": true,
     "steps": [
      {
       "label": "Start the point",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "First of all, let's think about [note 1].",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "To begin with, [note 1] matters because",
         "h": "+ a sentence"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "job": "Note 2 · a reason + an example",
     "label": "Paragraph 3",
     "words": 40,
     "support": true,
     "steps": [
      {
       "label": "Start the point",
       "route": "say",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "Another point to consider is [note 2].",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "Apart from that, [note 2] is also important because",
         "h": "+ a sentence"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Turn to the other side",
       "route": "both",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "On the other hand, we should also think about [note 2].",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "However, some people feel that",
         "h": "+ a sentence"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "job": "Your own idea",
     "label": "Paragraph 4",
     "words": 40,
     "support": true,
     "steps": [
      {
       "label": "Add your idea",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "Finally, I would add one more point: [your idea].",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "Something people often forget is [your idea]."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "job": "Your answer · commit to it",
     "label": "Conclusion",
     "words": 25,
     "steps": [
      {
       "label": "Decide",
       "route": "say",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "To sum up, I firmly believe that",
         "h": "+ your answer, mainly because + a sentence",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "All in all, it seems clear to me that",
         "h": "+ your answer"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Decide",
       "route": "both",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "All things considered, I believe that",
         "h": "+ your answer, mainly because + a sentence",
         "go": true
        },
        {
         "t": "Having looked at both sides, I think that",
         "h": "+ your answer"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "model": {
    "question": "‘All students should have to do sport at school.’ Do you agree? · Notes: learning teamwork · some people hate sport · your own idea",
    "route": "say",
    "paras": [
     "{People often disagree about} making sport compulsory at school. {In my opinion,} every student should do some sport, even those who are not very sporty.",
     "{First of all, let's think about} learning teamwork. {This is because} in a team game you have to listen, share and trust other people. {For example,} my basketball team taught me more about patience than any lesson.",
     "{Another point to consider is} the idea that some people hate sport. That is true, but schools could offer choices such as dance, swimming or yoga, so that everyone finds something they enjoy.",
     "{Finally, I would add one more point:} health. Many teenagers spend hours sitting in front of screens. {As a result,} a few hours of exercise a week can make a real difference to how they feel.",
     "{To sum up, I firmly believe that} sport should be compulsory, {mainly because} it keeps us healthy and teaches us to work together."
    ]
   },
   "tip": "Turn the question into a short [topic] before you start: ‘Should schools ban phones?’ → banning phones in schools."
  },
